    <section class="blocks-container glue-page glue-spacer-3-top">
      <div class="block">
          

<img
    class="banner-image"
    src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-developer-goog-blog-assets/images/argon__robotics__hero.original.png"
    alt="argon__robotics__hero"
/>  <div class="inner-block-content rich-content">
    <p data-block-key="te43t">Gemini 4 Argon marks a step change in physical understanding, code generation, and visual-semantic reasoning—unlocking new workflows across the robotics stack and accelerating progress toward physical AGI.</p><p data-block-key="6ndc1">You can see this leap in capability on the <a href="https://github.com/embodiedreasoning/ERQA">Embodied Reasoning (ERQA) benchmark</a>, which tests a model&#x27;s ability to understand and solve physical, spatial problems in 3D environments. Using pure reasoning, Argon scores 87%, outperforming every other frontier model.</p>
</div>   


    
    <div class="inner-block-content">
        <div class="image-wrapper">
            
                <img
                    class="regular-image"
                    src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-developer-goog-blog-assets/images/gemini-4-argon__benchmark__robotics.original.jpg"
                    alt="gemini-4-argon__benchmark__robotics"
                />
            
            
        </div>
    </div>
  <div class="inner-block-content rich-content">
    <p data-block-key="ji583">As a general-purpose physical reasoning model, Argon can be applied across the entire robotics lifecycle. In this post, we share representative prompts for Argon across four key areas:</p><p data-block-key="a31g2"></p><ul><li data-block-key="8jv6l"><b>Robot control →</b> Mobile manipulation with <a href="https://mujoco.org/">MuJoCo</a> practice, zero-shot robot control, and closed-loop steering of video world models.</li><li data-block-key="dhd8r"><b>Real2Sim →</b> Reconstructing physically calibrated simulation twins from robot camera feeds, egocentric human video, or hand-drawn paper sketches.</li><li data-block-key="7il3g"><b>Physical understanding →</b> Agentic multimodal hindsight labeling including detailed understanding of dexterity, dense value functions and progress estimation.</li><li data-block-key="amqbs"><b>Research and self-improvement →</b> Action improvement via simulation and iterative self-improvement on hardware.</li></ul><p data-block-key="1d7ei"></p><h2 data-block-key="7lro5" id="unlocking-robot-control-with-argon"><b>Unlocking robot control with Argon</b></h2><h3 data-block-key="2s7vg" id="1.-spot-mobile-manipulation:-putting-in-the-trash-bin-with-mujoco-practice"><b>1. Spot mobile manipulation: Putting in the trash bin with MuJoCo practice</b></h3><p data-block-key="dam3">Argon controls a Boston Dynamics Spot® quadruped (12-DoF legs + 6-DoF arm) to learn a new skill: stepping on a foot-pedal trash bin to throw away soda cans. Argon creates an articulated MuJoCo digital twin of a foot-pedal trash bin to practice its moves before stepping on the physical pedal and dropping soda cans into the open bin.</p>
</div>   

<div class="inner-block-content video-block">
    
        <video  autoplay="" loop="" muted="" playsinline="" poster="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-developer-goog-blog-assets/original_videos/wagtailvideo-ftsxdd1g_thumb.jpg">
<source src='https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-developer-goog-blog-assets/original_videos/Spot-can-long-voiceover-preview.mp4' type='video/mp4'>
<p>Sorry, your browser doesn't support playback for this video</p>

</video>
    
    
        
            <div class="video-description">Spot Mobile Manipulation — Real-to-Sim-to-Real foot-pedal trash bin disposal: Spot picking up the soda can, checking its wrist camera, practicing 3-leg tripod balance in MuJoCo, stepping on the foot pedal, verifying hand centering in the open bin, and dropping the can inside.</div>
        
    
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content rich-content">
    <p data-block-key="je901"><i>Prompt:</i></p>
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content code-block line-numbers">
    <pre><code class="language-plaintext">There&#x27;s a Diet Coke can behind you and another on the black table on your left.
Use the spot-mobile-manipulation skill to pick them up and trash them in the black foot-pedal bin.
Before stepping down on the pedal, verify in the front cameras that your front-right foot target is centered on the pedal, and use a 2-agent verification swarm (foot-verifier and hand-verifier) to verify both the foot-pedal step and the 3D hand-in-bin alignment before releasing.</code></pre>
    <div class="language-block glue-font-weight-medium">
        Plain text
    </div>
