    <div class="dark-mode-block">
        <button class="dark-mode-toggle">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" height="24px" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" width="24px" fill="#202124"><path d="M480-120q-150 0-255-105T120-480q0-150 105-255t255-105q14 0 27.5 1t26.5 3q-41 29-65.5 75.5T444-660q0 90 63 153t153 63q55 0 101-24.5t75-65.5q2 13 3 26.5t1 27.5q0 150-105 255T480-120Zm0-80q88 0 158-48.5T740-375q-20 5-40 8t-40 3q-123 0-209.5-86.5T364-660q0-20 3-40t8-40q-78 32-126.5 102T200-480q0 116 82 198t198 82Zm-10-270Z"/></svg>
        </button>
    </div>
    
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content rich-content">
    <h3 data-block-key="ygf0c" id="3.-omni-control"><b>3. Omni control</b></h3><p data-block-key="1n8tv">Argon steers robots in the Gemini Omni World Model to rearrange five scattered Scrabble tiles (<code>G, R, A, N, O</code>) into a clean row spelling <code>A - R - G - O - N</code>. Instead of specifying one static prompt, Argon steers in a closed visual loop. It writes timestamped action prompts, inspecting intermediate rollout keyframes, and refining its prompts.</p>
</div>   

<div class="inner-block-content video-block">
    
        <video  autoplay="" loop="" muted="" playsinline="" poster="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-developer-goog-blog-assets/original_videos/wagtailvideo-fxg62uyb_thumb.jpg">
<source src='https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-developer-goog-blog-assets/original_videos/omni_control_final_2.mp4' type='video/mp4'>
<p>Sorry, your browser doesn't support playback for this video</p>

</video>
    
    
        
            <div class="video-description">Iterative Video World Model Steering Dexterous Hands: 33-Step Steered Video Rollout Spelling A-R-G-O-N.</div>
        
    
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content rich-content">
    <p data-block-key="ji583"><i>Prompt:</i></p>
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content code-block line-numbers">
    <pre><code class="language-plaintext">Goal: {task_goal}

You are steering a video world model (Gemini Omni) in an iterative visual feedback loop. Inspect the attached frames from the latest rollout and write the next timestamped action prompt for the video world model:
- Break complex motions into one simple, single-direction action at a time.
- Keep inactive hands retracted and avoid blocking the camera&#x27;s view of objects in the workspace.
- Explicitly state which areas of the workspace become empty after an object moves.
- Use [MM:SS.mmm] timestamps for each action beat and wrap your output in &lt;omni_prompt&gt; tags.

Example format (sample timestamps only, not the full prompt):
&lt;omni_prompt&gt;
[00:00.000] Character A&#x27;s left hand rests at the side while the right hand reaches toward the target object.
[00:02.500] Character A&#x27;s right fingertips push the object smoothly into the center of the table, leaving its starting area empty.
[00:05.000] Character A&#x27;s right hand opens and retracts to the side so all placed objects remain in clear view of the camera.
&lt;/omni_prompt&gt;</code></pre>
    <div class="language-block glue-font-weight-medium">
        Plain text
    </div>
    <div class="copy-code-block">
        <span class="hidden">Copied</span>
        <button class="copy-clipboard">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" height="24px" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" width="24px" fill="#202124"><path d="M360-240q-33 0-56.5-23.5T280-320v-480q0-33 23.5-56.5T360-880h360q33 0 56.5 23.5T800-800v480q0 33-23.5 56.5T720-240H360Zm0-80h360v-480H360v480ZM200-80q-33 0-56.5-23.5T120-160v-560h80v560h440v80H200Zm160-240v-480 480Z"/></svg>
