        </button>
    </div>
    
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content rich-content">
    <h3 data-block-key="iawtk" id="2.-human-view-to-simulation"><b>2. Human view to simulation</b></h3><p data-block-key="ca57v">Given an egocentric human video of a manipulation task, Argon identifies the task-relevant objects, replaces crude bounding boxes with compound convex-decomposed meshes for concave containers, and retargets the human hand trajectory onto a 76-DoF bimanual humanoid with 22-DoF five-fingered hands in MuJoCo contact physics.</p>
</div>   

<div class="inner-block-content video-block">
    
        <video  autoplay="" loop="" muted="" playsinline="">
<source src='https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-developer-goog-blog-assets/original_videos/human_real2sim_2.mp4' type='video/mp4'>
<p>Sorry, your browser doesn't support playback for this video</p>

</video>
    
    
        
            <div class="video-description">Human View to Simulation — Egocentric Human Video to Dexterous Humanoid Twin: Left shows the input egocentric human RGB video; Right shows the synchronized 500 Hz MuJoCo + Blender Cycles multi-view simulation rollout.</div>
        
    
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content rich-content">
    <p data-block-key="f3ac8"><i>Prompt:</i></p>
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content code-block line-numbers">
    <pre><code class="language-plaintext">[Attached: egocentric_human_video.mp4, candidate_sim_views.png, hand_3d_keypoints.json]

You are building a physically solvable 500 Hz MuJoCo manipulation environment (`scene.xml`) and studio Blender render that faithfully reproduces the tabletop task shown in `egocentric_human_video.mp4` on a bimanual humanoid robot with 22-DoF dexterous five-fingered hands:

1. Scene Reconstruction &amp; Camera Calibration:
   - Identify only the manipulation-relevant objects (the grasped target object and the receiving container or landmark) and triangulate their 3D tabletop coordinates from the egocentric camera intrinsics/extrinsics.
   - Replace crude bounding boxes with compound convex-decomposed 3D meshes so concave containers (nested bowls, recessed wooden trays, open bins) support physical interior placement.

2. 500 Hz Dexterous Motion-Fitting Stress Test:
   - Retarget the 3D human wrist and finger keypoints to the humanoid&#x27;s 7-DoF arm and 22-DoF hand joints, and step the trajectory in MuJoCo at 500 Hz (dt = 0.002s) with zero kinematic weld constraints.
   - Verify opposing thumb-and-finger force closure, clean object lift (&gt; 2 cm), and stable final placement inside or beside the target landmark.</code></pre>
    <div class="language-block glue-font-weight-medium">
        Plain text
    </div>
    <div class="copy-code-block">
        <span class="hidden">Copied</span>
        <button class="copy-clipboard">
