        </button>
    </div>
    
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content rich-content">
    <h3 data-block-key="ddyd4" id="3.-sketch-to-simulation"><b>3. Sketch to simulation</b></h3><p data-block-key="3i6m2">With Argon, a developer can snap a photo of a rough pen-and-paper sketch—showing an Apollo 2 humanoid throwing a ball along a parabolic arc to topple a 3-2-1 stack of boxes on a table—and have Argon automatically construct the GPU-accelerated <code>mujoco_warp</code> scene, synthesize a balanced 76-DoF whole-body and five-finger throw trajectory, verify 6/6 target knockdown in closed-loop physics, and export a Blender 4.5 Cycles render.</p>
</div>   

<div class="inner-block-content video-block">
    
        <video  autoplay="" loop="" muted="" playsinline="">
<source src='https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-developer-goog-blog-assets/original_videos/sketch_to_sim_final.mp4' type='video/mp4'>
<p>Sorry, your browser doesn't support playback for this video</p>

</video>
    
    
        
            <div class="video-description">Sketch to Simulation — Hand-Drawn Sketch to Dexterous Humanoid Trajectory &amp; Cycles Render.</div>
        
    
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content rich-content">
    <p data-block-key="je901"><i>Prompt:</i></p>
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content code-block line-numbers">
    <pre><code class="language-plaintext">[Attached: hand_drawn_throw_sketch.jpg]

Translate this hand-drawn sketch into a physically verified humanoid simulation in `mujoco_warp` and a raytraced Blender Cycles video:

1. Scene &amp; Kinematic Setup from Sketch:
   - Parse the spatial layout from `hand_drawn_throw_sketch.jpg`: place the 76-DoF humanoid (32-DoF body equipped with two 22-DoF five-finger dexterous hands) at the origin facing a table holding a 3-2-1 pyramid of 6 rigid target boxes, with a projectile sphere grasped in the right five-finger hand.

2. Whole-Body Balance &amp; Dexterous Throw Synthesis:
   - Synthesize a 50 Hz whole-body throwing trajectory (140 steps, 2.80 s) across four phases: (1) stable stance &amp; 5-finger power grasp closure, (2) torso/shoulder wind-up with ankle-hip Center-of-Mass compensation, (3) forward whipping acceleration, and (4) synchronized 22-DoF five-finger opening at peak hand velocity so the ball launches on a ballistic arc into the pyramid&#x27;s second-tier center of mass.
   - Verify in `mujoco_warp` contact physics that the humanoid maintains upright balance (&lt; 3 cm pelvis drift) and knocks down all 6 target boxes.</code></pre>
    <div class="language-block glue-font-weight-medium">
        Plain text
    </div>
