</div>  <div class="inner-block-content rich-content">
    <h2 data-block-key="wnkv4" id="unlocking-physical-understanding-with-argon"><b>Unlocking physical understanding with Argon</b></h2><h3 data-block-key="e1tie" id="1.-hindsight-labeling-and-data-quality"><b>1. Hindsight labeling and data quality</b></h3><p data-block-key="65glh">Argon has precise physical understanding of dexterous manipulation and can provide detailed segmentation and text labeling from video. Argon is able to identify poor manipulation segments such as pauses, unstable grasps and fumbles. Given an overhead video of a bimanual ALOHA 2 robot folding a square sheet of paper into an origami fox over 136 seconds, Argon produces a time-aligned 4-level hindsight annotation hierarchy: Episode Goal (G1), 6 contiguous Semantic Subtasks (G2), 17 contact-level Atomic Primitives (G3), and automated Quality Control (QC) reweighting that holds task progress flat during fumbles and retries.</p>
</div>   

<div class="inner-block-content video-block">
    
        <video  autoplay="" loop="" muted="" playsinline="" poster="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-developer-goog-blog-assets/original_videos/wagtailvideo-qskcbv9x_thumb.jpg">
<source src='https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-developer-goog-blog-assets/original_videos/aloha2_origami_hindsight_1.mp4' type='video/mp4'>
<p>Sorry, your browser doesn't support playback for this video</p>

</video>
    
    
        
            <div class="video-description">Argon Multi-Granularity Hindsight &amp; Telemetry HUD.</div>
        
    
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content rich-content">
    <p data-block-key="mnjhj"><i>Prompt:</i></p>
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content code-block line-numbers">
    <pre><code class="language-plaintext">[Attached: Aloha2_Origami_20250309.mp4]

Produce a time-aligned multi-granularity hindsight annotation JSON with four levels:
1. G1_episode_instruction: Concise imperative sentence describing the overall manipulation goal.
2. G2_subtasks: Contiguous semantic subtask phases specifying which arm(s) anchor vs. fold/rotate the object.
3. G3_atomic_primitives: Fine-grained contact-level primitives (3–15s) aligned with grasp closure, crease sweeps, release, or retry attempts.
4. quality_control_and_reweighting: Hold task_progress_pct flat during non-progressing slip/delamination retry loops and downweight them (0.15x–0.25x) for Behavior Cloning.</code></pre>
    <div class="language-block glue-font-weight-medium">
        Plain text
    </div>
    <div class="copy-code-block">
        <span class="hidden">Copied</span>
        <button class="copy-clipboard">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" height="24px" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" width="24px" fill="#202124"><path d="M360-240q-33 0-56.5-23.5T280-320v-480q0-33 23.5-56.5T360-880h360q33 0 56.5 23.5T800-800v480q0 33-23.5 56.5T720-240H360Zm0-80h360v-480H360v480ZM200-80q-33 0-56.5-23.5T120-160v-560h80v560h440v80H200Zm160-240v-480 480Z"/></svg>
        </button>
    </div>
