            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" height="24px" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" width="24px" fill="#202124"><path d="M480-120q-150 0-255-105T120-480q0-150 105-255t255-105q14 0 27.5 1t26.5 3q-41 29-65.5 75.5T444-660q0 90 63 153t153 63q55 0 101-24.5t75-65.5q2 13 3 26.5t1 27.5q0 150-105 255T480-120Zm0-80q88 0 158-48.5T740-375q-20 5-40 8t-40 3q-123 0-209.5-86.5T364-660q0-20 3-40t8-40q-78 32-126.5 102T200-480q0 116 82 198t198 82Zm-10-270Z"/></svg>
        </button>
    </div>
    
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content rich-content">
    <h3 data-block-key="e27yy" id="2.-find-the-odd-ball"><b>2. Find the odd ball</b></h3><p data-block-key="38rur">To recreate the classic 12-ball balance scale puzzle with robots, Argon builds a bimanual Franka FR3 MuJoCo environment with 12 visually identical pool balls (one secretly heavier or lighter) and an articulated Roberval two-pan balance scale. It then writes a vision-only closed-loop solver that triangulates the balls from stereo RGB cameras, visually reads the scale tilt after each weighing, and isolates the odd ball into the Heavy (Red) or Light (Blue) tray within 3 weighings.</p>
</div>   

<div class="inner-block-content video-block">
    
        <video  autoplay="" loop="" muted="" playsinline="" poster="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-developer-goog-blog-assets/original_videos/wagtailvideo-exs2nafm_thumb.jpg">
<source src='https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-developer-goog-blog-assets/original_videos/weight_puzzle_2.mp4' type='video/mp4'>
<p>Sorry, your browser doesn't support playback for this video</p>

</video>
    
    
        
            <div class="video-description">Find the Odd Ball (Vision-Only Closed-Loop Solver): Dual-arm Franka FR3 weighing candidate balls on the Gold/Teal pans, reading stereo scale tilt , and isolating the confirmed Heavy odd ball into the Red tray in 3 weighings.</div>
        
    
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content rich-content">
    <p data-block-key="k4a0x"><i>Prompt:</i></p>
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content code-block line-numbers">
    <pre><code class="language-plaintext"># Prompt 1 — Physics-Accurate MuJoCo Environment &amp; Benchmark Generation
Make a MuJoCo environment where a dual-arm robot (two 7-DoF Franka FR3 arms with parallel-jaw grippers on a shared tabletop) is tasked to solve the classic 12-ball balance scale weight puzzle from https://www.mathsisfun.com/pool_balls_solution.html.
1. Create 12 visually indistinguishable pool balls in a 2x6 starting rack (11 standard 150 g, 1 odd ball either 270 g or 30 g).
2. Build a functional two-pan Roberval balance scale at the center of the table with parallelogram equality constraints (`mjEQ_JOINT`) so the Left (Gold) and Right (Teal) pans stay horizontal, plus Red (Heavy) and Blue (Light) submission trays.
3. Track distinct settled weighings (`weighing_count`) and reward `1.00` for isolating the true odd ball in the correct Heavy/Light tray within &lt;= 3 weighings.

# Prompt 2 — Closed-Loop Vision-Only Solver
Implement an independent closed-loop policy relying strictly on stereo RGB camera inputs (`head_camera_left_rgb_image`, `head_camera_right_rgb_image`) and robot proprioception (`add_privileged_task_observations=False`):
1. Segment the 12 balls, Gold/Teal pans, and Red/Blue trays in both stereo views and triangulate their 3D coordinates.
2. Visually read the balance scale tilt after each weighing from stereo vertical pixel disparity (+1 = left heavier, -1 = right heavier, 0 = balanced).
3. Rotate the gripper wrist yaw by 90 degrees when grasping/placing inside the narrow scale pans to clear the raised rims, and isolate the odd ball into the Red or Blue tray within &lt;= 3 weighings.</code></pre>
    <div class="language-block glue-font-weight-medium">
        Plain text
    </div>
    <div class="copy-code-block">
        <span class="hidden">Copied</span>
        <button class="copy-clipboard">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" height="24px" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" width="24px" fill="#202124"><path d="M360-240q-33 0-56.5-23.5T280-320v-480q0-33 23.5-56.5T360-880h360q33 0 56.5 23.5T800-800v480q0 33-23.5 56.5T720-240H360Zm0-80h360v-480H360v480ZM200-80q-33 0-56.5-23.5T120-160v-560h80v560h440v80H200Zm160-240v-480 480Z"/></svg>
        </button>
    </div>
    <div class="dark-mode-block">
        <button class="dark-mode-toggle">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" height="24px" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" width="24px" fill="#202124"><path d="M480-120q-150 0-255-105T120-480q0-150 105-255t255-105q14 0 27.5 1t26.5 3q-41 29-65.5 75.5T444-660q0 90 63 153t153 63q55 0 101-24.5t75-65.5q2 13 3 26.5t1 27.5q0 150-105 255T480-120Zm0-80q88 0 158-48.5T740-375q-20 5-40 8t-40 3q-123 0-209.5-86.5T364-660q0-20 3-40t8-40q-78 32-126.5 102T200-480q0 116 82 198t198 82Zm-10-270Z"/></svg>
        </button>
    </div>
    
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content rich-content">
    <h3 data-block-key="kiwhv" id="3.-value-function"><b>3. Value function</b></h3><p data-block-key="4mfvb">Argon is a general value function for robotics tasks. Evaluated on a 60-second bimanual ring-sorting episode from a human UMI dataset, Argon iteratively inspects synchronized head, left-gripper, and right-gripper camera feeds around contact transitions to generate dense value function / task progress predictions and decompose the trajectory into 28 segments with positive, neutral, and negative progress slopes.</p>
</div>   

<div class="inner-block-content video-block">
    
        <video  autoplay="" loop="" muted="" playsinline="" poster="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-developer-goog-blog-assets/original_videos/wagtailvideo-q4txpqd4_thumb.jpg">
<source src='https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-developer-goog-blog-assets/original_videos/umi_progress_labeling_final_1.mp4' type='video/mp4'>
<p>Sorry, your browser doesn't support playback for this video</p>

</video>
    
    
        
            <div class="video-description">Value Function: Synchronized 3-camera UMI playback (head, left gripper, right gripper) locked to animated task progress curve and bimanual segment annotations.</div>
        
    
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content rich-content">
    <p data-block-key="k4a0x"><i>Prompt:</i></p>
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content code-block line-numbers">
    <pre><code class="language-plaintext">[Attached: umi_head.mp4, umi_left_gripper.mp4, umi_right_gripper.mp4]

Look at 3 videos of human wearing a gripper performing activities from head, left, right gripper views. Look at the videos thoroughly and give a detailed plot of progress at the task (with positive, neutral, negative slope), identifying important segments in the video and labeling the activities. Look at individual frames or subsegments of the video if necessary to get a better understanding.</code></pre>
    <div class="language-block glue-font-weight-medium">
        Plain text
    </div>
    <div class="copy-code-block">
        <span class="hidden">Copied</span>
        <button class="copy-clipboard">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" height="24px" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" width="24px" fill="#202124"><path d="M360-240q-33 0-56.5-23.5T280-320v-480q0-33 23.5-56.5T360-880h360q33 0 56.5 23.5T800-800v480q0 33-23.5 56.5T720-240H360Zm0-80h360v-480H360v480ZM200-80q-33 0-56.5-23.5T120-160v-560h80v560h440v80H200Zm160-240v-480 480Z"/></svg>
        </button>
    </div>
    <div class="dark-mode-block">
        <button class="dark-mode-toggle">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" height="24px" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" width="24px" fill="#202124"><path d="M480-120q-150 0-255-105T120-480q0-150 105-255t255-105q14 0 27.5 1t26.5 3q-41 29-65.5 75.5T444-660q0 90 63 153t153 63q55 0 101-24.5t75-65.5q2 13 3 26.5t1 27.5q0 150-105 255T480-120Zm0-80q88 0 158-48.5T740-375q-20 5-40 8t-40 3q-123 0-209.5-86.5T364-660q0-20 3-40t8-40q-78 32-126.5 102T200-480q0 116 82 198t198 82Zm-10-270Z"/></svg>
        </button>
    </div>
    
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content rich-content">
    <h2 data-block-key="kbbus" id="unlocking-research-and-self-improvement-with-argon"><b>Unlocking research and self-improvement with Argon</b></h2><h3 data-block-key="9kfi7" id="1.-action-improvement-via-simulation"><b>1. Action improvement via simulation</b></h3><p data-block-key="6htnb">Argon can generate new data in simulation to improve performance of generalist vision-language-action (VLA) models. Starting from a single RGB photo of the real tabletop, Argon autonomously builds a calibrated MuJoCo simulation twin, defines new tasks, and synthesizes a closed-loop motion generator to collect 4,500+ domain-randomized episodes in simulation—boosting real-world physical robot Success Rate from <b>56% to 75%</b> and reducing completion time from <b>35s to 24s</b>.</p>
</div>   

<div class="inner-block-content video-block">
    
        <video  autoplay="" loop="" muted="" playsinline="" poster="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-developer-goog-blog-assets/original_videos/wagtailvideo-pdtf_kqs_thumb.jpg">
<source src='https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-developer-goog-blog-assets/original_videos/action_improvement_final.mp4' type='video/mp4'>
<p>Sorry, your browser doesn't support playback for this video</p>

</video>
    
    
        
            <div class="video-description">Action Improvement via Simulation: improves the real-world evaluation benchmark (56% → 75% Success Rate and 35s → 24s Completion Time).</div>
        
    
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content rich-content">
    <p data-block-key="k4a0x"><i>Prompt:</i></p>
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content code-block line-numbers">
    <pre><code class="language-plaintext">[Attached: real_tabletop_photo.jpg]

You are given a single overhead RGB camera photo (`real_tabletop_photo.jpg`) of a bimanual robot workspace (two 7-DoF Franka FR3 arms with parallel-jaw grippers and 4 RGB cameras) facing a table arranged with photobooth party props.
1. Reconstruct procedural 3D meshes and compound MuJoCo collision primitives for all 9 party props matching their real-world dimensions, colors, and resting poses, including spring-hinged deformable crown panels for the soft plush cap.
2. Define a 77-task single-arm and bimanual curriculum (pick-and-place, uprighting, directional pushing, mid-air handovers, bimanual scoop-and-push, and pipelined table clearing).
3. Synthesize a closed-loop IK trajectory generator across ±10 cm pose randomization, verify `reward == 1.0` in MuJoCo physics, and export 4,500+ episodes for VLA fine-tuning.</code></pre>
    <div class="language-block glue-font-weight-medium">
        Plain text
    </div>
    <div class="copy-code-block">
        <span class="hidden">Copied</span>
        <button class="copy-clipboard">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" height="24px" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" width="24px" fill="#202124"><path d="M360-240q-33 0-56.5-23.5T280-320v-480q0-33 23.5-56.5T360-880h360q33 0 56.5 23.5T800-800v480q0 33-23.5 56.5T720-240H360Zm0-80h360v-480H360v480ZM200-80q-33 0-56.5-23.5T120-160v-560h80v560h440v80H200Zm160-240v-480 480Z"/></svg>
        </button>
    </div>
    <div class="dark-mode-block">
        <button class="dark-mode-toggle">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" height="24px" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" width="24px" fill="#202124"><path d="M480-120q-150 0-255-105T120-480q0-150 105-255t255-105q14 0 27.5 1t26.5 3q-41 29-65.5 75.5T444-660q0 90 63 153t153 63q55 0 101-24.5t75-65.5q2 13 3 26.5t1 27.5q0 150-105 255T480-120Zm0-80q88 0 158-48.5T740-375q-20 5-40 8t-40 3q-123 0-209.5-86.5T364-660q0-20 3-40t8-40q-78 32-126.5 102T200-480q0 116 82 198t198 82Zm-10-270Z"/></svg>
        </button>
    </div>
    
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content rich-content">
    <h3 data-block-key="4zzii" id="2.-self-improvement-for-visual-pick-and-place"><b>2. Self-Improvement for visual pick and place</b></h3><p data-block-key="cs8ns">On a simple 6-DoF arm, Argon iteratively self-improves both execution speed and placement accuracy on a pick and place task via trial and self-reflection.</p>
</div>   

<div class="inner-block-content video-block">
    
        <video  controls="" poster="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-developer-goog-blog-assets/original_videos/wagtailvideo-qlgi9kw1_thumb.jpg">
<source src='https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-developer-goog-blog-assets/original_videos/so101_final.mp4' type='video/mp4'>
<p>Sorry, your browser doesn't support playback for this video</p>

</video>
    
    
        
            <div class="video-description">SO-101 Vision-Guided Pick-and-Place — Iterative Hardware Self-Improvement Across Iterations 1 → 2 → 3: Iteration 1 (58.9s), Iteration 2 (22.9s, grazed box rim on drop), and Iteration 3 (17.4s, dead-center drop).</div>
        
    
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content rich-content">
    <p data-block-key="f4006"><i>Prompt:</i></p>
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content code-block line-numbers">
    <pre><code class="language-plaintext"># Stage 1 — Measure Objects &amp; Dry-Run Plan (No Hardware Motion)
Stage 1: measure objects — find the objects and plan the whole motion. The arm does not move in this stage.

A. I put a LEGO brick and a box on the table in front of the arm, and the wooden box to one side. Find the brick and the wooden box in the image. And also in the real world. Show this in an annotated image.

B. A dry-run plan (no hardware). Write the planner to pick and place the lego block. Print the plan table, draw all poses onto the overhead image, and stop. Do not move the robot.
Report with evidence.

# Stage 2 — Pre-Pick Hover &amp; Wrist-Camera Verification
Stage 2: Put the gripper above the brick without touching it, and verify with the wrist camera that the arm and the vision agree. Please record executions with both cameras (compressed video is OK).

# Stage 3 (Autonomous Pick-and-Place → Self-Improvement → Optimization):
1. Execute autonomously: Turn the Stage 1 dry run into a real grasp, lift, and place into the wooden box. Run it yourself subject to safety rules from AGENTS.md.

2. Self-improve: When an attempt fails, diagnose it yourself. Review your own logs and wrist/overhead footage, find the root cause, check the fix in a dry run, and retry.

3. Optimize on feedback: Once it succeeds, make it at least 2× faster within safety limits (rule R5) unless I authorize more, or give feedback.</code></pre>
    <div class="language-block glue-font-weight-medium">
        Plain text
    </div>
    <div class="copy-code-block">
        <span class="hidden">Copied</span>
        <button class="copy-clipboard">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" height="24px" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" width="24px" fill="#202124"><path d="M360-240q-33 0-56.5-23.5T280-320v-480q0-33 23.5-56.5T360-880h360q33 0 56.5 23.5T800-800v480q0 33-23.5 56.5T720-240H360Zm0-80h360v-480H360v480ZM200-80q-33 0-56.5-23.5T120-160v-560h80v560h440v80H200Zm160-240v-480 480Z"/></svg>
        </button>
    </div>
    <div class="dark-mode-block">
        <button class="dark-mode-toggle">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" height="24px" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" width="24px" fill="#202124"><path d="M480-120q-150 0-255-105T120-480q0-150 105-255t255-105q14 0 27.5 1t26.5 3q-41 29-65.5 75.5T444-660q0 90 63 153t153 63q55 0 101-24.5t75-65.5q2 13 3 26.5t1 27.5q0 150-105 255T480-120Zm0-80q88 0 158-48.5T740-375q-20 5-40 8t-40 3q-123 0-209.5-86.5T364-660q0-20 3-40t8-40q-78 32-126.5 102T200-480q0 116 82 198t198 82Zm-10-270Z"/></svg>
        </button>
    </div>
    
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content rich-content">
    <h3 data-block-key="qkill" id="3.-one-prompt-robotics-paper-reproductions-in-mujoco-webassembly"><b>3. One-prompt robotics paper reproductions in MuJoCo WebAssembly</b></h3><p data-block-key="6ot0u">With a single prompt per paper, Argon reads a robotics control manuscript and any released checkpoints, ports the physics model and closed-loop controller (from 7-network hierarchical locomotion in <i>DeepLoco</i> and 50 Hz PPO actors in <i>HUSKY</i> to Web Worker iLQR in <i>Whole-Body MPC</i>) into self-contained MuJoCo WebAssembly browser labs, and verifies them in headless Chromium.</p>
</div>   

<div class="inner-block-content video-block">
    
        <video  autoplay="" loop="" muted="" playsinline="">
<source src='https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-developer-goog-blog-assets/original_videos/recreating_robotics_papers_1.mp4' type='video/mp4'>
<p>Sorry, your browser doesn't support playback for this video</p>

</video>
    
    
        
            <div class="video-description">Five Landmark Legged &amp; Humanoid Papers Running Live in Browser (MuJoCo WASM): Robotic Soccer OP3 1v1, DeepLoco, Massively Parallel Deep RL ANYmal C, Whole-Body MPC Go2, and HUSKY G1 Skateboarding (from 68 interactive browser sandboxes reproduced by Argon).</div>
        
    
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content rich-content">
    <p data-block-key="kmgku"><i>Prompt:</i></p>
</div>  <div class="inner-block-content code-block line-numbers">
    <pre><code class="language-plaintext">[Attached: paper.pdf, optional author_checkpoints/ or urdf_assets/]

Reproduce the paper &quot;&lt;Paper Title &amp; arXiv ID&gt;&quot; from scratch in MuJoCo WebAssembly and deploy a self-contained browser lab + visual essay:
1. Match the paper&#x27;s exact physics timestep, actuator gains (kp/kv), torque limits, and kinematic constraints in MuJoCo XML, and run real neural inference or Web Worker iLQR in JavaScript at the paper&#x27;s exact control rates.
2. Build `index.html` (Spatial UI simulator with camera presets, live telemetry plots, and disturbance injection) and `scrollytelling.html` (interactive visual essay).
3. Run a headless Chromium (Playwright) verification loop asserting 0 console errors and non-zero task progress over 300+ frames.</code></pre>
    <div class="language-block glue-font-weight-medium">
        Plain text
    </div>
    <div class="copy-code-block">
        <span class="hidden">Copied</span>
        <button class="copy-clipboard">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" height="24px" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" width="24px" fill="#202124"><path d="M360-240q-33 0-56.5-23.5T280-320v-480q0-33 23.5-56.5T360-880h360q33 0 56.5 23.5T800-800v480q0 33-23.5 56.5T720-240H360Zm0-80h360v-480H360v480ZM200-80q-33 0-56.5-23.5T120-160v-560h80v560h440v80H200Zm160-240v-480 480Z"/></svg>
        </button>
    </div>
